<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG Chem in export deal with SmithKline. [CORRECTED 08:56 GMT]</title>
<headline>LG Chem in export deal with SmithKline. [CORRECTED 08:56 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's LG Chemical Ltd, a unit of the LG Group, said on Monday it has signed a contract with SmithKline Beecham Plc to export its antibiotic manufacturing technology to the British company.</p>
<p>LG will receive signing and milestone payments of up to approximately $38 million, plus attractive royalties on sales of the medicine to be produced using the technology, an LG official said, without giving further details (company corrects details).</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the technology was for the manufacture of a fluoroquinolone antibiotic.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
